  {
   "say": "This is a perfect quality of life. Israel is here.",
   "gap": 0.2
  },
  {
   "say": "Ninety-two out of a hundred, on the UN's Human Development Index. Health, education, income.",
   "gap": 0.12
  },
  {
   "say": "What's in the gap? Poverty: one in five Israelis.",
   "screen": "*20.7%* of Israelis poor",
   "gap": 0.12
  },
  {
   "say": "Prices: fourth highest of thirty-eight rich countries.",
   "screen": "*4th* highest prices of 38 OECD countries",
   "gap": 0.12
  },
  {
   "say": "And Israel is only twenty-seventh. Iceland is first.",
   "screen": "Israel *27th*. Iceland *1st*",
   "gap": 0.15
  },
  {
   "say": "Now zoom out. They picture Israel as a poor, backward place.",
   "gap": 0.12
  },
  {
   "say": "Poor and backward looks like this: around sixty-six, the UN's average for medium development.",
   "screen": "*66* = UN average, medium development",
   "gap": 0.15
  },
  {
   "say": "The Emirates, ninety-four. Saudi Arabia, ninety. Turkey, eighty-five. Iran, eighty. Jordan and Egypt, seventy-five. Lebanon, seventy-five.",
   "screen": "Same scale. *The region.*",
   "gap": 0.15,
   "until": "L7e+0.3"
  },
  {
   "say": "Only one neighbour is closer to utopia.",
   "gap": 0.15
  },
  {
   "say": "One honest catch: the Emirates beat us. Fifteenth in the world.",
   "gap": 0.15
  },
  {
   "say": "We're not perfect. We know it.",
   "gap": 0.12
  },
  {
   "say": "But poor and backward? Not even close."
  }
 ],
